cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use hw-apex-bench, cite this software and identify the exact commit or
  released version. When citing measurements, also identify their run and
  artifact hashes, codec configuration and host; results from distinct scopes
  are not interchangeable. Code is Apache-2.0; measurements are CC BY 4.0.
type: software
version: "0.1"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22713364"
date-released: "2026-09-11"
title: "hw-apex-bench: Compressed Access Benchmark"
authors:
  - name: "yasha1971-coder"
    website: "https://github.com/yasha1971-coder"
repository-code: "https://github.com/yasha1971-coder/hw-apex-bench"
url: "https://yasha1971-coder.github.io/hw-apex-bench/"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  An adapter-based harness for measuring compression ratio, encoding and full
  decoding throughput, regional access latency, decoding amplification,
  granularity cost, batch access, access entropy and break-even request counts.
  Results retain byte-exact verification, configuration, commands and provenance,
  with explicit reasons for unsupported measurements.
keywords:
  - compression
  - random access
  - benchmarking
  - reproducibility
  - bioinformatics
